# rule.always.externalize.lessons.into_briefs

the PARENT (the act is `enbrief`); zoom-ins by lesson kind:

| the lesson is about | reach for | owes |
|---|---|---|
| a word (dobj/dop named, synonym argued) | `.for.domain.terms` | a `.reason` cluster |
| an invariant litigated | `.for.domain.invariants` | nature/nurture label + counter-argument |
| a glyph claimed or unregistered | `.for.domain.glyphs` | a catalog row |
| any other concept | this rule | — |

capture the ARGUMENT, never only the conclusion.

when you learn, write it down before context fades, into `.agent/repo=.this/role=*/briefs/`, short. cues: a concept surprised you · was hard to discover · you had to ask or research · you wish someone had told you sooner. test: *"would i want to know this if i were new here?"*

blocker: a lesson learned and not externalized.

see: `rule.require.timeless-lessons` (standard) · `rule.always.scope-onetime-lessons-to-the-behavior` (where).
